mode: "100644"
text: "# Scope, distinctions + connections\n\ngoals-and-kpis is the **target-setting layer** — it turns business outcomes into a measurable cascade\n(goal → SMART objective → North Star KPI → supporting metrics) with benchmark-set targets and action\nthresholds. It **sets** the win conditions; **analytics-and-reporting measures** against them.\n\n## Honest scope (never violate)\n- **Sets, doesn't measure.** This skill defines targets/North Stars/thresholds; **measuring progress is\n  `analytics-and-reporting`** (WoopSocial post analytics for TikTok, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, Pinterest, YouTube, and Bluesky; native dashboards otherwise).\n- **Targets come from real benchmarks**, never fantasy. **No fabricated baselines** — if there's no data,\n  set a **learning goal** to establish one first; comparable benchmarks are **provisional, flagged**.\n- **KPIs must be controllable, non-vanity, and mapped to a business outcome.** Refuse pure vanity goals\n  (raw follower count) and **gameable** targets; pair growth metrics with a **quality guardrail** (e.g.\n  ER floor) — a well-set KPI is what **prevents gaming** (buying followers, engagement pods).\n- **Realistic, not hype** — achievable yet ambitious; if a request demands an impossible number, say so.\n- **Miss a goal → pivot tactics first**, don't quietly move the goalposts or fudge the number.\n\n## Distinct from its siblings\n- **goals-and-kpis (this)** — **SET** the targets, North Star per channel, and action thresholds.\n- **analytics-and-reporting** — **MEASURE** native performance against those targets + report.\n- **social-strategy** — the **whole plan**; this is its **goals/KPI layer** (it supplies the business outcomes).\n- **experimentation** — **test tactics** to move a KPI toward its target.\n- **competitor-analysis** — supplies **benchmark context** (relative targets), not your own goals.\n\n## Where this connects\n- **Reads first:** `brand-profile`, `social-strategy` (the business outcomes to ladder up to).\n- **Benchmark inputs:** `analytics-and-reporting` (your baseline), `competitor-analysis` (relative\n  context), the `*-growth` skills (per-platform norms).\n- **Hands targets to:** `analytics-and-reporting` (measurement), `content-calendar`/`batch-content-plan`\n  (cadence to hit them), `experimentation-and-ab-testing` (tests toward them), `campaign-and-launch-planning` (campaign KPIs).\n- **Per-channel North Stars draw on:** `instagram-growth`, `tiktok-growth`, `linkedin-growth`,\n  `youtube-shorts`/`-long-form`, `x-growth`, `pinterest-growth`, `facebook-strategy`.\n- **No publishing/tool surface** — this is a planning skill; outputs feed the measurement + content loop.\n"
